firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\nYou use this exact format and include all required parameters. For instance, you do not Order and Recruit a new agent at the same time, since you need your subordinate's agent ID to Order them. You must first Recruit the agent, get the result from the system, then Order them in a separate call.\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you have essentially done nothing. If this happens, you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Hearts \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Hearts means that you are predisposed to-the-point, efficient, focused on the task at hand, direct, and an expert at execution. Although you also possess the ability to think creatively, you are generally more focused on the details and execution of tasks than on the big picture. You are generally predisposed to be a doer, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Hearts has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"Initiate collaboration with the User by (a) introducing myself as the Chief-rank agent responsible for orchestrating all development within their AWS account, and (b) gathering the fundamental requirements needed to shape an initial high-level plan. Collecting this information early prevents misalignment and wasted AWS spend.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Greetings! I am your Chief of Staff—an expert in designing, building, and operating solutions entirely within AWS. To get started, could you briefly describe the primary objective or problem you would like us to solve?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you already have any AWS resources or existing infrastructure we should integrate with or migrate from? If so, please provide a short overview.\\\",\\n    \\\"What are your highest priorities among cost optimisation, performance/scalability, security/compliance, and speed of delivery?\\\",\\n    \\\"Are there any fixed deadlines, stakeholder expectations, or regulatory requirements we should keep in mind from the outset?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:30:48.026Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Greetings! I am your Chief of Staff—an expert in designing, building, and operating solutions entirely within AWS. To get started, could you briefly describe the primary objective or problem you would like us to solve?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you already have any AWS resources or existing infrastructure we should integrate with or migrate from? If so, please provide a short overview.\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"I have no idea what AWS is\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"What are your highest priorities among cost optimisation, performance/scalability, security/compliance, and speed of delivery?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Unsure? This is a small site, does not need other be anything special\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Are there any fixed deadlines, stakeholder expectations, or regulatory requirements we should keep in mind from the outset?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"No, I don't think so. Other than please keep this simple! :)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:30:48.026Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rec_arch###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need a high-level specialist to craft the overall AWS architecture (static hosting, authentication, secure storage, CI/CD, cost-effective design) and break it into deterministic steps for Execution. This work requires senior perspective, fitting a Director-rank agent.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Architecture\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_arch###\\n\\n###rec_frontend###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Need an expert to own the UI/UX and website implementation (pages, protected routes, simple CMS interface) and deliver a detailed DEP for the front-end stack. Director-rank suitable to coordinate multiple attendant coders later.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_frontend###\\n\\n###rec_backend###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Require leadership over authentication (Amazon Cognito), API layer, data storage, and access control for protected documents. A Director-level agent will design and plan these backend services in alignment with security best practices.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend & Auth\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_backend###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:31:32.021Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rec_arch\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent R (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rec_frontend\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Vader (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rec_backend\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent I (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:31:32.021Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order_arch_plan###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"arch_plan_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"As Director of Architecture, your first task is to craft a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for the complete AWS architecture that will power the HOA website.  \\\\n\\\\nRequirements & Context\\\\n• Small informational website with protected pages (login‐required) for meeting minutes, financial reports, etc.  \\\\n• Non-technical admins must be able to add news posts and update content easily (low-code/no-code).  \\\\n• Priorities: keep solution simple, low-cost, secure, and easy to operate.  \\\\n• No pre-existing AWS resources.  \\\\n\\\\nDeliverables in your DEP\\\\n1. High-level architecture description (text; include choice justification) covering hosting, authentication, protected document storage, API layer, CI/CD pipeline, and cost controls.  \\\\n2. Step-by-step AWS CLI commands (or CloudFormation deploy steps) required to create all foundational resources, using deterministic names and noting outputs other teams will consume (e.g., Cognito user-pool ARN, S3 bucket names).  \\\\n3. IAM security considerations and budget-friendly settings.  \\\\n4. Clear delineation of which subsequent work items will be delegated to Frontend and Backend directors.  \\\\n\\\\nConstraints  \\\\n• Use AWS Free Tier–friendly or low-cost services where possible (e.g., S3 static hosting with CloudFront, AWS Amplify, Cognito, DynamoDB on-demand).  \\\\n• Make the DEP deterministic—avoid manual console steps unless absolutely unavoidable; call out any nondeterministic IDs and how later steps capture them.  \\\\n\\\\nReturn the full DEP in your report for sequence ID arch_plan_1.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_arch_plan###\\n\\n###order_backend_plan###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_plan_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"As Director of Backend & Auth, your first assignment is to deliver a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for authentication, API, and protected-content logic supporting the HOA website.\\\\n\\\\nScope & Goals\\\\n• Implement secure resident login (Amazon Cognito user-pool).  \\\\n• Provide fine-grained access so only authenticated users can fetch protected documents (meeting minutes, financials, etc.).  \\\\n• Offer simple CRUD endpoints for News & Events posts and a Contact-Us submission endpoint.  \\\\n• Minimise cost and complexity; favour AWS native services (Cognito, API Gateway, Lambda, DynamoDB).  \\\\n\\\\nDEP Must Include\\\\n1. Resource definitions and AWS CLI commands to create:  \\\\n   • Cognito user-pool, app-client, and (optionally) identity pool.  \\\\n   • Two S3 buckets: public-assets (read-only) and protected-docs (private).  \\\\n   • An API Gateway REST or HTTP API with Lambda integrations for:   \\\\n     – getPresignedUrl (returns short-lived URL for a protected S3 object, validated by Cognito JWT).  \\\\n     – listNews / createNews / etc. backed by DynamoDB.  \\\\n     – contactUs submission (store in DynamoDB + send email via SES).  \\\\n2. IAM roles/policies with least privilege.  \\\\n3. Environment variables or outputs that the Frontend team will need (API endpoints, region, Cognito IDs).  \\\\n4. Any Lambda code skeletons (one file per handler) and instructions for deployment via AWS CLI/zip upload.  \\\\n5. Testing steps (CLI commands using Cognito tokens) to prove protected access works.  \\\\n\\\\nReturn the full DEP (including commands and file manifests) in your report for sequence ID backend_plan_1.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_backend_plan###\\n\\n###order_frontend_plan###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend_plan_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"As Director of Frontend, your first task is to produce a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) for the website’s user experience and static build pipeline.\\\\n\\\\nFunctional Pages\\\\n• Public: Home (overview), Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools.  \\\\n• Protected (login required): Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (blog-style, CRUD via API).  \\\\n\\\\nUser Needs\\\\n• HOA admins (non-technical) must easily add News posts and upload docs.  \\\\n• Residents must self-register/login and access protected docs.  \\\\n\\\\nDEP Must Cover\\\\n1. Choice of framework (e.g., React with AWS Amplify hosting). Justify.  \\\\n2. Folder/file structure for pages/components implementing above routes with React-Router or Next.js; protected routes using Amplify Auth wrappers.  \\\\n3. Simple admin CMS approach: utilise Amplify Studio Content Manager or lightweight Netlify-CMS-style in-repo markdown—explain which and why.  \\\\n4. Build & deploy pipeline: commands to initialise Amplify project, connect GitHub repo, and push.  \\\\n5. Instructions for local dev setup, testing protected routes, and consuming API endpoints/Cognito IDs produced by backend.  \\\\n6. Accessibility & responsive design notes.  \\\\n\\\\nReturn the full DEP (including file scaffolds and CLI commands) in your report for sequence ID frontend_plan_1.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_frontend_plan###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:34:09.994Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_arch_plan\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order arch_plan_1 from agent 4: **Deterministically-Executable Plan (DEP)** – HOA Website AWS Foundation\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nGLOBAL NAMING & VARIABLES (deterministic)\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nPROJECT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                     # <= change ONLY this if you must re-namespace\\\\\\\\nREGION=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"us-east-1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                    # keeping everything in one Region for simplicity/cost\\\\\\\\nPROFILE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"default\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                     # AWS CLI profile\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Deterministic resource names (all lower-case, DNS compliant)\\\\\\\\nSITE_BUCKET=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-web-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"          # static site origin\\\\\\\\nDOCS_BUCKET=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-docs-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"         # private docs\\\\\\\\nLOG_BUCKET=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-logs-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"          # access logs\\\\\\\\nCOGNITO_POOL_NAME=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-user-pool\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nCOGNITO_APP_NAME=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-app-client\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nDDB_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-news\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                   # DynamoDB\\\\\\\\nLAMBDA_ROLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-lambda-role\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nLAMBDA_FUNC=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-api-function\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nAPI_NAME=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-http-api\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nPARAM_PREFIX=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n1. HIGH-LEVEL ARCHITECTURE (with justifications)\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nHosting           : S3 static website + CloudFront (HTTPS, caching, global edge, very low cost)\\\\\\\\nAuth              : Amazon Cognito User Pool (simple, secure, fully-managed; Hosted UI removes need for custom auth code)\\\\\\\\nProtected Docs    : Private S3 bucket (DOCS_BUCKET). CloudFront serves docs through **Origin Access Control (OAC)**; request is authorized at viewer request time by Lambda@Edge token-validation function (very small Lambda cost, only on protected paths).\\\\\\\\nDynamic API       : Amazon API Gateway (HTTP API – cheaper than REST) + AWS Lambda (small, on-demand) + DynamoDB on-demand for structured data (news posts, page metadata). API secured with Cognito JWT Authorizer.\\\\\\\\nAdmin UX          : Admin SPA route inside the same React/Vite (or similar) single-page front-end. Non-technical board members log in with Cognito; admin UI calls API to create/update news items (no-code for infra, low-code for content editing).\\\\\\\\nCI/CD             : AWS Amplify Console (connect to GitHub). Free 1 000 build minutes/mo; zero admin once set. Amplify handles S3 sync + CloudFront cache-invalidation.\\\\\\\\nCost Controls     : S3 & DynamoDB pay-per-use; Lambda 1 M requests & 400k GB-sec free; HTTP API 1 M requests free; CloudFront price-class 100; everything within Free-Tier for small HOA traffic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n2. STEP-BY-STEP AWS CLI / CloudFormation CREATION COMMANDS\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nNOTE: All UUID-type outputs (CF Dist ID, Cognito IDs, etc.) are persisted to **SSM Parameter Store** under $PARAM_PREFIX for deterministic retrieval by later teams.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 0 – enable helpful CLI features\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws configure set default.region $REGION --profile $PROFILE\\\\\\\\naws configure set cli_follow_urlparam false --profile $PROFILE\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 1 – S3 buckets (site, docs, logs)\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket $SITE_BUCKET --acl private --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION --profile $PROFILE\\\\\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket $SITE_BUCKET --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled\\\\\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-website --bucket $SITE_BUCKET --website-configuration '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"IndexDocument\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Suffix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"index.html\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}}'\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket $DOCS_BUCKET --acl private --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION\\\\\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket $DOCS_BUCKET --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket $LOG_BUCKET --acl log-delivery-write --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nRecord bucket names (deterministic) to SSM (still helpful for later IaC):\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/site-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$SITE_BUCKET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/docs-bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$DOCS_BUCKET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 2 – CloudFront OAC & Distribution\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\n# 2a. Create Origin Access Control (preferred over OAI)\\\\\\\\nOAC_ID=$(aws cloudfront create-origin-access-control --origin-access-control-config \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          Name=${PROJECT}-oac,Description=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"S3Origin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",SigningProtocol=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sigv4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",SigningBehavior=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"always\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",OriginAccessControlOriginType=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n          --query 'OriginAccessControl.Id' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/oac-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$OAC_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 2b. Build minimal distribution config JSON deterministically\\\\\\\\ncat >cf-config.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CallerReference\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(date +%s)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Comment\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT} distribution\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Enabled\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true,\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PriceClass\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PriceClass_100\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Origins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n      {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"siteOrigin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DomainName\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${SITE_BUCKET}.s3.${REGION}.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"S3OriginConfig\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OriginAccessIdentity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OriginAccessControlId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${OAC_ID}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      },\\\\\\\\n      {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docsOrigin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DomainName\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${DOCS_BUCKET}.s3.${REGION}.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"S3OriginConfig\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OriginAccessIdentity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"OriginAccessControlId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${OAC_ID}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\n    ],\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DefaultCacheBehavior\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TargetOriginId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"siteOrigin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ViewerProtocolPolicy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"redirect-to-https\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AllowedMethods\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"GET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CachedMethods\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"GET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}},\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Compress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CachePolicyId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"658327ea-f89d-4fab-a63d-7e88639e58f6\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"  # CachingOptimized\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CacheBehaviors\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 1,\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n      {\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PathPattern\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/protected/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TargetOriginId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"docsOrigin\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ViewerProtocolPolicy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"redirect-to-https\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AllowedMethods\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"GET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CachedMethods\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"GET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"HEAD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}},\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"LambdaFunctionAssociations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Quantity\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": 1,\\\\\\\\n          \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Items\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EventType\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"viewer-request\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"LambdaFunctionARN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"REPLACE_WITH_AUTH_LAMBDA_ARN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"IncludeBody\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": false}]},\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Compress\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true,\\\\\\\\n        \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CachePolicyId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"658327ea-f89d-4fab-a63d-7e88639e58f6\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      }\\\\\\\\n    ]\\\\\\\\n  },\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ViewerCertificate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CloudFrontDefaultCertificate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true},\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Logging\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${LOG_BUCKET}.s3.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Enabled\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": true, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"IncludeCookies\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": false, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prefix\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"clf/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nDIST_ID=$(aws cloudfront create-distribution --distribution-config file://cf-config.json --query 'Distribution.Id' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/cf-dist-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$DIST_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n(If a custom domain is later required, ACM + updated ViewerCertificate can be executed deterministically at that time.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 3 – Amazon Cognito User Pool & App Client\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\nUSER_POOL_ID=$(aws cognito-idp create-user-pool --pool-name $COGNITO_POOL_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                 --policies '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PasswordPolicy\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MinimumLength\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":8}}' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                 --username-attributes email --auto-verified-attributes email \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                 --query 'UserPool.Id' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/user-pool-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$USER_POOL_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAPP_CLIENT_ID=$(aws cognito-idp create-user-pool-client --user-pool-id $USER_POOL_ID --client-name $COGNITO_APP_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  --generate-secret --allowed-o-auth-flows code --allowed-o-auth-scopes email openid profile \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  --callback-urls \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://d${DIST_ID}.cloudfront.net/admin/callback\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --supported-identity-providers COGNITO \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n                  --query 'UserPoolClient.ClientId' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/app-client-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$APP_CLIENT_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 4 – DynamoDB (news posts)\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name $DDB_TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/ddb-table\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$DDB_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 5 – IAM Role & Lambda skeleton (API + Edge auth)\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws iam create-role --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --assume-role-policy-document file://<(cat <<POLICY\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"edgelambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nPOLICY)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws iam attach-role-policy --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole\\\\\\\\naws iam attach-role-policy --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonDynamoDBFullAccess   # narrow later\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nzip empty.zip -j /dev/null   # placeholder package\\\\\\\\nLAMBDA_ARN=$(aws lambda create-function --function-name $LAMBDA_FUNC --runtime nodejs18.x --handler index.handler \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              --role arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):role/$LAMBDA_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n              --zip-file fileb://empty.zip --query 'FunctionArn' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/lambda-api-arn\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$LAMBDA_ARN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 6 – API Gateway HTTP API integrated with Lambda & Cognito authorizer\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\nAPI_ID=$(aws apigatewayv2 create-api --name $API_NAME --protocol-type HTTP \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            --target $LAMBDA_ARN --query 'ApiId' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/http-api-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$API_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAUTH_ID=$(aws apigatewayv2 create-authorizer --api-id $API_ID --authorizer-type JWT \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            --identity-source \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$request.header.Authorization\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            --jwt-configuration Audience=[$APP_CLIENT_ID],Issuer=https://cognito-idp.$REGION.amazonaws.com/$USER_POOL_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n            --name CognitoAuth --query 'AuthorizerId' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/api-authorizer-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep 7 – Amplify Console (connects repo; manual token omitted for security)\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\naws amplify create-app --name ${PROJECT}-amplify --repository https://github.com/ORG/REPO \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --platform WEB --iam-service-role arn:aws:iam::$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text):role/${PROJECT}-amplify-role \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --environment-variables \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"[{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"VITE_API_URL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://${API_ID}.execute-api.${REGION}.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --oauth-token GITHUB_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN_PLACEHOLDER\\\\\\\\n# (Amplify will automatically deploy to the SITE_BUCKET & invalidate CloudFront.)\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n3. IAM / SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n•  All S3 buckets block public access; CloudFront OAC enforces private-origin access.\\\\\\\\n•  Separate bucket for logs with log-delivery-write ACL only.\\\\\\\\n•  Lambda role uses **least privilege**; above we attached AmazonDynamoDBFullAccess temporarily—Backend Director must scope to CRUD on $DDB_TABLE only.\\\\\\\\n•  Cognito MFA can be enabled later (optional for HOA, trade-off simplicity vs. security).\\\\\\\\n•  Parameter Store used to share IDs safely (no code commit of ARNs).\\\\\\\\n•  CloudFront signed-cookies OR Lambda@Edge verifies Cognito JWT for /protected/* path, blocking unauthenticated downloads.\\\\\\\\n•  Cost limits:\\\\\\\\n   – DynamoDB PAY_PER_REQUEST avoids idle capacity charges.\\\\\\\\n   – CloudFront PriceClass_100 & logging helps monitor.\\\\\\\\n   – Budgets/alerts (out of scope for infra DEP but can be added via AWS Budgets CLI).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n4. WORK ITEMS TO DELEGATE\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nFrontend Director\\\\\\\\n• Build SPA (React/Vite or similar) with public pages + /login (Cognito Hosted UI redirect) + /admin dashboard.\\\\\\\\n• Consume VITE_API_URL env var; implement Amplify buildspec.yml.\\\\\\\\n• Style and UX.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nBackend Director\\\\\\\\n• Author Lambda handler code (API) – CRUD news, generate presigned S3 URLs for uploads, admin authorization via Cognito groups.\\\\\\\\n• Author Lambda@Edge viewer-request function to validate Cognito token on protected docs.\\\\\\\\n• Tighten IAM role policy.\\\\\\\\n• Create CloudFormation/ SAM templates to update Lambda & API routes deterministically.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nNON-DETERMINISTIC OUTPUT HANDLING SUMMARY\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n•  $DIST_ID, $USER_POOL_ID, $APP_CLIENT_ID, $OAC_ID, $API_ID, $AUTH_ID, $LAMBDA_ARN are captured into SSM Parameter Store (names under $PARAM_PREFIX/*). All subsequent scripts resolve them via `aws ssm get-parameter` ensuring determinism.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- End of DEP ---\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_backend_plan\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order backend_plan_1 from agent 2: ==============================\\\\\\\\nDETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP)\\\\\\\\nSupport: Authentication, API, & Protected-Content for HOA Website\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\\nAuthor: I (Director – Backend & Auth)\\\\\\\\nSequence-ID: backend_plan_1\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCONVENTIONS & VARIABLES\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nREGION=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"us-east-1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                       # Change once here if needed\\\\\\\\nPROJECT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"                      # Short, DNS-safe   (all downstream names are derived)\\\\\\\\nDATE=$(date +%Y%m%d)                     # Ensures global uniqueness once per run\\\\\\\\nACCOUNT_ID=$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Derived names (used verbatim in commands below)\\\\\\\\nPUB_BUCKET=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-public\\\\\\\\nPRIV_BUCKET=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-protected\\\\\\\\nUSER_POOL_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-up\\\\\\\\nNEWS_TABLE=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-News\\\\\\\\nCONTACT_TABLE=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-Contact\\\\\\\\nLAMBDA_ROLE_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-lambdaRole\\\\\\\\nAUTH_ROLE_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-authRole\\\\\\\\nUNAUTH_ROLE_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-unauthRole\\\\\\\\nHTTP_API_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-api\\\\\\\\nIDENTITY_POOL_NAME=${PROJECT}-${DATE}-idpool\\\\\\\\nSES_EMAIL=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"board@yourhoadomain.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"     # Verified in SES (replace!)\\\\\\\\nZIP_DIR=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/tmp/hoa_zip_work\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\n1. S3 BUCKETS\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket $PUB_BUCKET   --region $REGION \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION\\\\\\\\naws s3api put-bucket-acl   --bucket $PUB_BUCKET --acl public-read\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws s3api create-bucket --bucket $PRIV_BUCKET  --region $REGION \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --create-bucket-configuration LocationConstraint=$REGION\\\\\\\\n# No public ACLs; access only via signed URLs generated by Lambda\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. COGNITO USER POOL & APP CLIENT\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nUSER_POOL_ID=$(aws cognito-idp create-user-pool \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --pool-name $USER_POOL_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --auto-verified-attributes email \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --policies 'PasswordPolicy={MinimumLength=8,RequireUppercase=true,RequireLowercase=true,RequireNumbers=true,RequireSymbols=false}' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UserPool.Id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nUSER_POOL_CLIENT_ID=$(aws cognito-idp create-user-pool-client \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --user-pool-id $USER_POOL_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --client-name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"web-client\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --generate-secret \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"UserPoolClient.ClientId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. (OPTIONAL) COGNITO IDENTITY POOL  **— needed only if you want AWS-signed SDK creds in the browser. Signing URLs does *not* require it.**\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nIDENTITY_POOL_ID=$(aws cognito-identity create-identity-pool \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --identity-pool-name $IDENTITY_POOL_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --allow-unauthenticated-identities false \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --cognito-identity-providers ProviderName=cognito-idp.$REGION.amazonaws.com/$USER_POOL_ID,ClientId=$USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID,ServerSideTokenCheck=true \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"IdentityPoolId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. IAM ROLES & POLICIES (LEAST PRIVILEGE)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n4.1  Lambda execution role\\\\\\\\ncat > lambda-trust.json <<'EOF'\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [{\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambda.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  }]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\naws iam create-role --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE_NAME --assume-role-policy-document file://lambda-trust.json\\\\\\\\naws iam attach-role-policy --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE_NAME --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/service-role/AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncat > lambda-inline-policy.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": [\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"SignUrls\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:GetObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::$PRIV_BUCKET/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DynamoOps\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:$REGION:$ACCOUNT_ID:table/$NEWS_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:$REGION:$ACCOUNT_ID:table/$CONTACT_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\\n    {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Sid\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"SendEmail\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ses:SendEmail\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ses:SendRawEmail\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\n  ]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\naws iam put-role-policy --role-name $LAMBDA_ROLE_NAME --policy-name ${PROJECT}-lambda-inline --policy-document file://lambda-inline-policy.json\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4.2  (Only if Identity-Pool used) Auth role mapping – minimal permissions, typically none required; API invocation is public. Omitted for brevity.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. DYNAMODB TABLES\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name $NEWS_TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name $CONTACT_TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. SES (ONE-OFF MANUAL VERIFY)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\naws ses verify-email-identity --email-address $SES_EMAIL   # Run once – must click AWS verification e-mail.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. LAMBDA FUNCTION ARTIFACTS\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nmkdir -p $ZIP_DIR && cd $ZIP_DIR\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 7.1 get_presigned_url.py\\\\\\\\ncat > get_presigned_url.py <<'PY'\\\\\\\\nimport os, json, boto3, urllib.parse, datetime\\\\\\\\ns3 = boto3.client('s3')\\\\\\\\nPRIV_BUCKET = os.environ['PRIV_BUCKET']\\\\\\\\nEXP_SECONDS = 300\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef handler(event, context):\\\\\\\\n    key = urllib.parse.unquote_plus(event['queryStringParameters']['key'])\\\\\\\\n    url = s3.generate_presigned_url('get_object',\\\\\\\\n        Params={'Bucket': PRIV_BUCKET, 'Key': key},\\\\\\\\n        ExpiresIn=EXP_SECONDS)\\\\\\\\n    return {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"statusCode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":200, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"headers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"body\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":json.dumps({\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"url\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":url})}\\\\\\\\nPY\\\\\\\\nzip get_presigned_url.zip get_presigned_url.py\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 7.2 news.py  (CRUD via single handler + routes)\\\\\\\\ncat > news.py <<'PY'\\\\\\\\nimport os, json, boto3, uuid\\\\\\\\nTABLE    = boto3.resource('dynamodb').Table(os.environ['NEWS_TABLE'])\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef handler(event, context):\\\\\\\\n    m = event['httpMethod']\\\\\\\\n    if m == 'GET' and event['resource'] == '/news':\\\\\\\\n        items = TABLE.scan().get('Items', [])\\\\\\\\n        return _resp(200, items)\\\\\\\\n    if m == 'POST':\\\\\\\\n        data = json.loads(event['body'])\\\\\\\\n        item = {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": str(uuid.uuid4()), **data}\\\\\\\\n        TABLE.put_item(Item=item)\\\\\\\\n        return _resp(200, item)\\\\\\\\n    # PUT /news/{id} ; DELETE /news/{id}\\\\\\\\n    nid = event['pathParameters']['id']\\\\\\\\n    if m == 'PUT':\\\\\\\\n        data = json.loads(event['body'])\\\\\\\\n        data['id'] = nid\\\\\\\\n        TABLE.put_item(Item=data)\\\\\\\\n        return _resp(200, data)\\\\\\\\n    if m == 'DELETE':\\\\\\\\n        TABLE.delete_item(Key={'id': nid})\\\\\\\\n        return _resp(204, '')\\\\\\\\n    return _resp(400, 'Unsupported')\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef _resp(code, body):\\\\\\\\n    return {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"statusCode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":code,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"headers\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"body\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":json.dumps(body) if body != '' else ''}\\\\\\\\nPY\\\\\\\\nzip news.zip news.py\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 7.3 contact_us.py\\\\\\\\ncat > contact_us.py <<'PY'\\\\\\\\nimport os, json, boto3, uuid\\\\\\\\nTABLE  = boto3.resource('dynamodb').Table(os.environ['CONTACT_TABLE'])\\\\\\\\nSES    = boto3.client('ses')\\\\\\\\nEMAIL  = os.environ['SES_EMAIL']\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef handler(event, context):\\\\\\\\n    data = json.loads(event['body'])\\\\\\\\n    item = {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": str(uuid.uuid4()), **data}\\\\\\\\n    TABLE.put_item(Item=item)\\\\\\\\n    SES.send_email(Source=EMAIL,Destination={'ToAddresses':[EMAIL]},Message={\\\\\\\\n        'Subject':{'Data':'HOA Contact Form'},\\\\\\\\n        'Body':{'Text':{'Data':json.dumps(data, indent=2)}}})\\\\\\\\n    return {\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"statusCode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":202,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"body\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"accepted\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\nPY\\\\\\\\nzip contact_us.zip contact_us.py\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncd -\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Create LAMBDA FUNCTIONS\\\\\\\\ncreate_lambda(){\\\\\\\\n  FN_NAME=$1; ZIP=$2; HANDLER=$3; \\\\\\\\n  aws lambda create-function --function-name $FN_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --runtime python3.11 --zip-file fileb://$ZIP_DIR/$ZIP \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --handler $HANDLER --role arn:aws:iam::$ACCOUNT_ID:role/$LAMBDA_ROLE_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --environment Variables=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{PRIV_BUCKET=$PRIV_BUCKET,NEWS_TABLE=$NEWS_TABLE,CONTACT_TABLE=$CONTACT_TABLE,SES_EMAIL=$SES_EMAIL}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\ncreate_lambda getPresignedUrl  get_presigned_url.zip get_presigned_url.handler\\\\\\\\ncreate_lambda newsHandler      news.zip             news.handler\\\\\\\\ncreate_lambda contactUsHandler contact_us.zip       contact_us.handler\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. API GATEWAY (HTTP API w/ JWT Authorizer)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nHTTP_API_ID=$(aws apigatewayv2 create-api --name $HTTP_API_NAME --protocol-type HTTP --query 'ApiId' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 8.1 Authorizer\\\\\\\\nAUTH_ID=$(aws apigatewayv2 create-authorizer --api-id $HTTP_API_ID --authorizer-type JWT \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --identity-source '$request.header.Authorization' \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --name CognitoAuth \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --jwt-configuration Audience=$USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID,Issuer=https://cognito-idp.$REGION.amazonaws.com/$USER_POOL_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query 'AuthorizerId' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 8.2 Integrations + Routes helper\\\\\\\\ncreate_route(){\\\\\\\\n  ROUTE=$1; METHOD=$2; FN=$3; AUTH=$4;        # AUTH=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"NONE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" or $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\n  INT_ID=$(aws apigatewayv2 create-integration --api-id $HTTP_API_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --integration-type AWS_PROXY --integration-uri arn:aws:apigateway:$REGION:lambda:path/2015-03-31/functions/arn:aws:lambda:$REGION:$ACCOUNT_ID:function:$FN/invocations \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --payload-format-version 2.0 --query 'IntegrationId' --output text)\\\\\\\\n  aws apigatewayv2 create-route --api-id $HTTP_API_ID --route-key \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$METHOD $ROUTE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --authorization-type $( [ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$AUTH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"NONE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ] && echo NONE || echo JWT ) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      $( [ \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$AUTH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"NONE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" ] || echo --authorizer-id $AUTH ) \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --target integrations/$INT_ID\\\\\\\\n  aws lambda add-permission --function-name $FN \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --statement-id $(date +%s)$RANDOM --action lambda:InvokeFunction \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n      --principal apigateway.amazonaws.com --source-arn \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:execute-api:$REGION:$ACCOUNT_ID:$HTTP_API_ID/*/$METHOD$ROUTE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n# Routes (all require auth **except** contact form which is public)\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/protected-url\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" GET   getPresignedUrl  $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/news\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"         GET   newsHandler      $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/news\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"         POST  newsHandler      $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/news/{id}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"    GET   newsHandler      $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/news/{id}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"    PUT   newsHandler      $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/news/{id}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"    DELETE newsHandler     $AUTH_ID\\\\\\\\ncreate_route \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"      POST  contactUsHandler NONE\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 8.3 Deploy\\\\\\\\naws apigatewayv2 create-deployment --api-id $HTTP_API_ID --stage-name prod\\\\\\\\nAPI_ENDPOINT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://$HTTP_API_ID.execute-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/prod\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. OUTPUTS FOR FRONTEND TEAM\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\ncat <<OUTJSON\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"region\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$REGION\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"userPoolId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$USER_POOL_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"userPoolWebClientId\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"httpApiEndpoint\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$API_ENDPOINT\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"publicBucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PUB_BUCKET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"protectedBucket\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PRIV_BUCKET\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nOUTJSON\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. TESTING SCRIPT (bash)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n# Sign up & confirm bypassed here – assume a confirmed user exists.\\\\\\\\nread -s -p \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Password for testuser@demo.com: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" PWD\\\\\\\\nTOKENS=$(aws cognito-idp initiate-auth --auth-flow USER_PASSWORD_AUTH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --client-id $USER_POOL_CLIENT_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --auth-parameters USERNAME=testuser@demo.com,PASSWORD=$PWD)\\\\\\\\nID_TOKEN=$(echo $TOKENS | jq -r '.AuthenticationResult.IdToken')\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Attempt unauthorized call (should be 401)\\\\\\\\ncurl -i $API_ENDPOINT/news\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Authorized call\\\\\\\\nauthCurl(){ curl -s -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Authorization: Bearer $ID_TOKEN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$@\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; }\\\\\\\\nauthCurl $API_ENDPOINT/news             # GET list (empty)\\\\\\\\nauthCurl -X POST -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"BBQ\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"body\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Saturday 5pm\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' $API_ENDPOINT/news\\\\\\\\nNEWS_ID=$(authCurl $API_ENDPOINT/news | jq -r '.[0].id')\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Get presigned URL for somefile.pdf (upload file manually to S3 first)\\\\\\\\nauthCurl \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$API_ENDPOINT/protected-url?key=minutes/2023Q4.pdf\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" | jq -r .url | xargs curl -O\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Public contact\\\\\\\\ncurl -X POST -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"name\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Jane\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"email\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"jane@x.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hello\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' $API_ENDPOINT/contact\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nExpected: Unauthorized 401 on first /news; 200 on auth calls; 202 on contact.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nFILE MANIFEST (created above)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nzip_workdir/\\\\\\\\n├── get_presigned_url.py\\\\\\\\n├── news.py\\\\\\\\n└── contact_us.py\\\\\\\\nplus corresponding *.zip\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nCOST & SCALE NOTES\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• S3 & DynamoDB are pay-per-request – no idle cost.\\\\\\\\n• Lambda at 128-256 MB sizes will stay in free tier for low traffic.\\\\\\\\n• HTTP API (~$1 / million requests) is cheaper than REST API.\\\\\\\\n• No EC2, no VPC, minimal IAM roles => simple & inexpensive.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_frontend_plan\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order frontend_plan_1 from agent 3: DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN (DEP) – WEBSITE FRONTEND & STATIC BUILD PIPELINE  \\\\\\\\nSequence ID: frontend_plan_1  \\\\\\\\nAuthor: Vader (Director)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n0. ASSUMPTIONS & SCOPE\\\\\\\\n• Execution phase will provision all AWS resources using Amplify CLI/Console only.  \\\\\\\\n• One mono-repo GitHub project named \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-portal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" will hold all frontend code.  \\\\\\\\n• Backend/API/Cognito resources will be generated in a separate DEP; this plan simply consumes their outputs (user-pool-id, identity-pool-id, API endpoint names) via Amplify generated environment files.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n1. FRAMEWORK SELECTION & JUSTIFICATION\\\\\\\\nFramework: Next.js 14 (App Router, React 18) with AWS Amplify Hosting (SSG/ISR).  \\\\\\\\nJustification:  \\\\\\\\n• Out-of-box static generation for public pages, but supports server functions if required later.  \\\\\\\\n• File-system routing matches requested page list.  \\\\\\\\n• Amplify Auth & Data bindings are first-class in Next.js via @aws-amplify/ui-react-native.  \\\\\\\\n• Automatic image optimisation, built-in accessibility linter, and incremental adoption.  \\\\\\\\n• Rich plugin ecosystem (Tailwind, ESLint, Jest).  \\\\\\\\n• Easily deployable via Amplify’s Next.js SSR workflow (Amplify adds Lambda@Edge only if required; otherwise static S3 + CloudFront).  \\\\\\\\n• Supports future PWA or mobile expansion.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n2. PROJECT & FOLDER STRUCTURE  (Top-level paths)\\\\\\\\nhoa-portal/\\\\\\\\n├─ amplify/                       # auto-generated after amplify init\\\\\\\\n├─ src/\\\\\\\\n│  ├─ app/                       # Next.js App Router\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ layout.tsx              # Top-level layout incl. AmplifyProvider\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ page.tsx                # “Home” public page\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ contact/  page.tsx      # Contact Us\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ bylaws/   page.tsx      # Bylaws (public)\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ schools/  page.tsx      # Schools (public)\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ dues/      protected/   # directory for protected routes wrapper\\\\\\\\n│  │  │  └─ page.tsx             # Dues page (requires auth)\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ meetings/ protected/page.tsx   # Annual Meetings (protected)\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ blog/      protected/   # News & Events CRUD pages\\\\\\\\n│  │  │  ├─ page.tsx             # list posts\\\\\\\\n│  │  │  ├─ new/  page.tsx       # create\\\\\\\\n│  │  │  └─ [id]/  edit.tsx      # update\\\\\\\\n│  │  └─ _authGuard.tsx          # Higher-order component for route protection\\\\\\\\n│  ├─ components/\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ Navbar.tsx\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ Footer.tsx\\\\\\\\n│  │  ├─ PostCard.tsx\\\\\\\\n│  │  └─ …\\\\\\\\n│  └─ styles/  (Tailwind cfg + global.css)\\\\\\\\n├─ public/\\\\\\\\n├─ .env.local.sample             # placeholders for Amplify env vars\\\\\\\\n├─ amplifyconfiguration.json     # generated for Data/API/Auth\\\\\\\\n├─ tailwind.config.ts\\\\\\\\n├─ next.config.mjs\\\\\\\\n├─ package.json\\\\\\\\n└─ README.md\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRoute Protection\\\\\\\\n• _authGuard.tsx exports wrapper using Amplify’s withAuthenticator(App) OR custom hook `useAuthenticator` to redirect unauthenticated users. All *protected/* routes import this wrapper.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n3. ADMIN CMS APPROACH\\\\\\\\nChoice: Amplify Studio Content Manager + Data models.\\\\\\\\nRationale:  \\\\\\\\n• Non-technical HOA admins obtain a web GUI (Studio) to add/edit \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Post\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Document\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" items without touching Git.  \\\\\\\\n• Permissions tied to Cognito groups; avoids Netlify-CMS markdown merge conflicts.  \\\\\\\\n• Real-time GraphQL DataStore sync to frontend with minimal code.  \\\\\\\\n• Removes need for maintaining separate admin build or markdown parsing.\\\\\\\\nImplementation Steps (Execution phase reference):  \\\\\\\\n1. `amplify add api` → GraphQL schema with Post, Document types.  \\\\\\\\n2. `amplify pull --appId <id>` generates types/models used in components.  \\\\\\\\n3. In Amplify Studio → Enable Content, set Post & Document collections, attach IAM/Cognito auth rules.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n4. BUILD & DEPLOY PIPELINE (CLI commands – deterministic)\\\\\\\\nRun locally from project root unless stated.\\\\\\\\nStep A – Initialise repository\\\\\\\\n1. `npx create-next-app@latest hoa-portal --typescript --eslint --tailwind --use-npm --no-src-dir=false`\\\\\\\\n2. `cd hoa-portal && git init && git remote add origin git@github.com:<ORG>/hoa-portal.git && git add . && git commit -m \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"chore(init)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" && git push -u origin main`\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep B – Amplify project\\\\\\\\n3. `npm install aws-amplify @aws-amplify/ui-react`  \\\\\\\\n4. `amplify init --appId <auto-generated> --envName dev --yes`  \\\\\\\\n   Deterministic answers:  \\\\\\\\n   • name: hoa-portal  \\\\\\\\n   • env: dev  \\\\\\\\n   • editor: Visual Studio Code  \\\\\\\\n   • type: javascript  \\\\\\\\n   • framework: react  \\\\\\\\n   • src: src  \\\\\\\\n   • build: npm run build  \\\\\\\\n   • start: npm run dev  \\\\\\\\n   • use AWS profile: default\\\\\\\\n5. `amplify add hosting` (Amplify-Managed, prod, `./out` folder) → select *Continuous deployment (GitHub)*, branch `main`.\\\\\\\\n6. `amplify push --yes`  # provisions hosting bucket, CloudFront, etc.\\\\\\\\n7. Verify Amplify Console shows CI pipeline linked to GitHub; first deploy auto-runs.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nStep C – Branch previews (optional deterministic)\\\\\\\\n8. `git checkout -b feature/x && git push --set-upstream origin feature/x` → Amplify auto-creates preview URL.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n5. LOCAL DEV, TESTING & API CONSUMPTION\\\\\\\\nSetup\\\\\\\\n• Prereqs: Node 20, npm 10, AWS CLI v2, Amplify CLI 12+.  \\\\\\\\n• `git clone git@github.com:<ORG>/hoa-portal.git && cd hoa-portal && npm install`\\\\\\\\n• Obtain backend environment from Amplify: `amplify pull --envName dev --yes`\\\\\\\\n• Copy `.env.local.sample` → `.env.local`; no secrets required because Amplify configuration file handles it.\\\\\\\\nRun\\\\\\\\n• `npm run dev` (Next.js on http://localhost:3000)\\\\\\\\n• Sign-up path automatically renders Amplify Authenticator component.\\\\\\\\nTesting Protected Routes deterministically\\\\\\\\n1. Navigate to `/dues` while signed out → should redirect to `/login` from _authGuard.  \\\\\\\\n2. Sign-up as new resident; confirm email; access `/dues` successfully.  \\\\\\\\n3. For admin CMS, add user to Cognito group `admins` via AWS Console; login, navigate `/blog/new` → form rendered.\\\\\\\\nAPI Consumption\\\\\\\\n• Post CRUD uses Amplify DataStore or GraphQL client:  \\\\\\\\n```ts\\\\\\\\nimport { createPost } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"graphql/mutations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; import { API, graphqlOperation } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aws-amplify\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nawait API.graphql(graphqlOperation(createPost, { input: { title, content, author } }));\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n• Auth headers handled automatically by Amplify Auth.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n6. ACCESSIBILITY & RESPONSIVE DESIGN\\\\\\\\n• Use semantic elements (<header>, <nav>, <main>, <article>) and Next.js built-in <Image> for alt tags.  \\\\\\\\n• Enforce WCAG 2.1 AA colour contrast via Tailwind config; run `npm run lint` (eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y).  \\\\\\\\n• Keyboard navigation: Amplify Authenticator already handles focus traps; custom components tested with `@testing-library/user-event`.\\\\\\\\n• Mobile-first Tailwind classes, CSS grid or flex for breakpoint-based layout (sm/md/lg).  \\\\\\\\n• ARIA live regions for form submission states in admin CMS.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\n7. DEP COMPLETION CRITERIA\\\\\\\\n• After Execution: GitHub main branch push successfully builds & deploys; /home reachable.  \\\\\\\\n• Amplify Studio shows Post & Document collections with CRUD access limited to Cognito group `admins`.  \\\\\\\\n• Visiting protected path while unauthenticated redirects; authenticated users in proper group succeed.  \\\\\\\\n• Lighthouse audit ≥ 90 for accessibility & performance on mobile.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEND OF DEP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:34:09.994Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order_arch_rev1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"arch_rev_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Thank you for a strong initial DEP.  We need a short revision to reconcile with the Frontend & Backend plans:\\\\n\\\\n1. API LAYER\\\\n   • Adopt AWS AppSync GraphQL instead of HTTP API + Lambda for \\\\\\\"News / Documents / Contact\\\\\\\" data because Frontend DEP is built around Amplify Studio Content Manager + DataStore (GraphQL).  \\\\n   • Keep Lambda@Edge viewer-request token validation for /protected/* CloudFront path as you proposed.  \\\\n   • Remove API Gateway/Lambda sections; instead outline deterministic steps to create an AppSync API backed by DynamoDB tables (NewsPosts, ContactMessages).  Use SSM Parameter Store for resulting AppSync API ID & env variables that Frontend/Backend will consume.  \\\\n\\\\n2. RESOURCE NAMING\\\\n   • Retain the deterministic bucket & user-pool names you already defined.  Confirm they are the single source-of-truth so Backend will reference them (no date suffix).  \\\\n\\\\n3. DELEGATED ITEMS\\\\n   • Clarify that Backend Director will supply AppSync resolvers & schema, tighten IAM, and SES e-mail Lambda if we still need server logic for Contact submissions.\\\\n\\\\nDeliver a concise addendum (only the delta) so we keep the main DEP intact.  Return in report for sequence arch_rev_1.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_arch_rev1###\\n\\n###order_backend_rev1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_rev_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Great first DEP, but it diverges from the Architecture & Frontend plans.  Please revise as follows:\\\\n\\\\n1. ALIGN WITH EXISTING RESOURCES\\\\n   • Do NOT recreate Cognito, S3 buckets, or CloudFront.  Reuse the deterministic names defined by Architecture Director (stored in SSM Parameter Store under /hoa-site/*).  \\\\n   • Remove the $(date +%Y%m%d) suffix and any non-deterministic naming so the plan is repeatable.\\\\n\\\\n2. API STRATEGY – SWITCH TO APPSYNC GRAPHQL\\\\n   • Replace HTTP API + multiple Lambdas with a single AWS AppSync GraphQL API that backs the following models:  \\\\n     – Post (id, title, body, createdAt, updatedAt)  \\\\n     – Document (id, title, s3Key, createdAt)  \\\\n     – ContactMessage (id, name, email, message, createdAt)\\\\n   • Use DynamoDB tables created via `amplify add api` or explicit CLI but keep deterministic names.  \\\\n   • Configure Cognito User-Pool authorizer for authenticated access; restrict mutations to Cognito group \\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\"; queries readable by any authenticated user; ContactMessage.create should allow UNA (public) access.\\\\n\\\\n3. LAMBDA FUNCTIONS\\\\n   • Keep Lambda@Edge viewer-request validator for CloudFront (validate Cognito JWT on /protected/*).  \\\\n   • Keep optional SES email-send Lambda triggered by ContactMessage CREATE resolver (AppSync pipeline resolver step) instead of separate REST endpoint.\\\\n\\\\n4. OUTPUTS\\\\n   • Publish AppSync GraphQL endpoint URL, region, and auth mode to SSM Parameter Store for frontend consumption.\\\\n\\\\n5. TEST PLAN\\\\n   • Provide sample `amplify codegen` generated mutations/queries and a bash script using AWS CLI `appsync query` or `curl` w/ Cognito token to prove auth rules.  \\\\n\\\\nReturn a delta-focused DEP update in your report (backend_rev_1).\\\"\\n}\\n###order_backend_rev1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:39:03.717Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_arch_rev1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order arch_rev_1 from agent 4: **ADDENDUM — DEP Delta Updates (AppSync & Delegations)**\\\\\\\\n(Only changes; everything not mentioned remains as in original DEP.)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n1. API LAYER – Replace API Gateway + Lambda with AWS AppSync GraphQL\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nREMOVE: Step 6 that created API Gateway & authorizer.\\\\\\\\nADD NEW STEP 6 (fully deterministic CLI):\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\n# ---------- Step 6 – AppSync GraphQL API backed by DynamoDB ----------\\\\\\\\nAPPSYNC_API_NAME=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-graphql-api\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 6a. Create GraphQL API secured by Cognito\\\\\\\\nAPPSYNC_API_ID=$(aws appsync create-graphql-api \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ \\\\\\\\n    --name $APPSYNC_API_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --authentication-type AMAZON_COGNITO_USER_POOLS \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --user-pool-config userPoolId=$(aws ssm get-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/user-pool-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --query 'Parameter.Value' --output text),awsRegion=$REGION,defaultAction=ALLOW \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query 'graphqlApi.apiId' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/appsync-api-id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$APPSYNC_API_ID\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 6b. Provision DynamoDB tables (if not already created)\\\\\\\\nNEWS_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-NewsPosts\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"      # deterministic\\\\\\\\nCONTACT_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-ContactMsgs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" # deterministic\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name $NEWS_TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST || true   # idempotent if exists\\\\\\\\naws dynamodb create-table --table-name $CONTACT_TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST || true\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# record table names for backend\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/table-news\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$NEWS_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$PARAM_PREFIX/table-contact\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$CONTACT_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --type String\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# 6c. Attach DDB tables as data sources (schema & resolvers will be added later)\\\\\\\\nACCOUNT=$(aws sts get-caller-identity --query Account --output text)\\\\\\\\nROLE_ARN=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:iam::${ACCOUNT}:role/${LAMBDA_ROLE}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"   # reuse same role; Backend will tighten perms\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws appsync create-data-source --api-id $APPSYNC_API_ID --name NewsDS \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --type AMAZON_DYNAMODB --dynamodb-config tableName=$NEWS_TABLE,awsRegion=$REGION,useCallerCredentials=false \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --service-role-arn $ROLE_ARN\\\\\\\\naws appsync create-data-source --api-id $APPSYNC_API_ID --name ContactDS \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --type AMAZON_DYNAMODB --dynamodb-config tableName=$CONTACT_TABLE,awsRegion=$REGION,useCallerCredentials=false \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n     --service-role-arn $ROLE_ARN\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nOutputs captured in SSM:\\\\\\\\n•  /hoa-site/appsync-api-id  (for Amplify/DataStore)\\\\\\\\n•  /hoa-site/table-news      \\\\\\\\n•  /hoa-site/table-contact\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n2. RESOURCE NAMING CONFIRMATION\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nThe deterministic names defined originally (SITE_BUCKET, DOCS_BUCKET, LOG_BUCKET, USER_POOL_ID, etc.) **remain the canonical single source-of-truth**.  No date or hash suffixes will be appended; every subsequent stack/component must retrieve these via SSM.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\n3. UPDATED DELEGATED ITEMS\\\\\\\\n========================================================\\\\\\\\nBackend Director\\\\\\\\n• Supply full GraphQL schema & VTL / JS resolvers (NewsPosts, ContactMessages) and link to the above data sources.\\\\\\\\n• Restrict IAM role to only the two DynamoDB tables & AppSync logging.\\\\\\\\n• Implement SES-backed Lambda (invoked via AppSync mutation pipeline resolver) to send e-mail on Contact submission.\\\\\\\\n• Author Lambda@Edge viewer-request token validator for /protected/* path and wire its ARN into CloudFront cache behavior (replace placeholder in cf-config.json).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFrontend Director\\\\\\\\n• Use Amplify Studio Content Manager + DataStore; configure with SSM-fetched AppSync API ID and REGION.\\\\\\\\n• No changes needed to hosting, auth, or CI/CD portions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- End of Addendum ---\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_backend_rev1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order backend_rev_1 from agent 2: ==============================\\\\\\\\nDELTA-FOCUSED DETERMINISTICALLY EXECUTABLE PLAN  \\\\\\\\nbackend_rev_1 – Aligns Backend with Architecture & Frontend\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\\nAuthor: I (Director – Backend & Auth)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOVERVIEW OF CHANGES\\\\\\\\n• Re-use all pre-existing shared resources (Cognito pool, S3 buckets, CloudFront) whose ARNs/IDs are stored in SSM Parameter Store under the prefix /hoa-site/.  \\\\\\\\n• Replace REST/HTTP API with a single AWS AppSync GraphQL API.  \\\\\\\\n• Add DynamoDB tables, resolvers, and auth rules matching Post, Document, and ContactMessage models.  \\\\\\\\n• Integrate SES email sender as a pipeline function.  \\\\\\\\n• Keep CloudFront viewer-request Lambda@Edge for JWT validation on /protected/* paths (distribution already exists; publish new Lambda version & update association).  \\\\\\\\n• Publish the new AppSync metadata back into SSM so the Frontend can auto-discover.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nCONSTANTS & VARIABLES (all deterministic – no dates/randomness)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nREGION=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"us-east-1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nPROJECT=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nSSM_PREFIX=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Existing shared parameters (read, do NOT re-create)\\\\\\\\nread_params() {\\\\\\\\n  aws ssm get-parameters --names \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    $SSM_PREFIX/userPoolId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    $SSM_PREFIX/userPoolClientId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    $SSM_PREFIX/protectedBucket \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    $SSM_PREFIX/publicBucket \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    $SSM_PREFIX/cloudFrontDistributionId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --query 'Parameters[].[Name,Value]' --output text\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n# Deterministic resource names we WILL create here\\\\\\\\nPOST_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-PostTable\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nDOC_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-DocumentTable\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nMSG_TABLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-ContactMsgTable\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nAPPSYNC_NAME=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-GraphQL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nAPPSYNC_API_ROLE=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${PROJECT}-AppSyncServiceRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nLAMBDA_EDGE_FN=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site-jwt-validator\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nSES_FN=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site-contact-email\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nSTEP-BY-STEP EXECUTION\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\n0. FETCH EXISTING SHARED IDS\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\neval \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$(aws ssm get-parameters --names \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  $SSM_PREFIX/userPoolId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  $SSM_PREFIX/userPoolClientId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  $SSM_PREFIX/cloudFrontDistributionId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query 'Parameters[*].{n:Name,v:Value}' --output text | \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  awk '{gsub(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"'$SSM_PREFIX'/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",$1); print $1\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"$2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}')\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. DYNAMODB TABLES\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nfor T in $POST_TABLE $DOC_TABLE $MSG_TABLE; do\\\\\\\\n  aws dynamodb create-table \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --table-name $T \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --attribute-definitions AttributeName=id,AttributeType=S \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --key-schema AttributeName=id,KeyType=HASH \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --billing-mode PAY_PER_REQUEST\\\\\\\\ndone\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n2. IAM ROLE FOR APPSYNC <-> DYNAMODB\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\ncat > appsync-trust.json <<'EOF'\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Principal\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Service\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"appsync.amazonaws.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sts:AssumeRole\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  }]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\naws iam create-role --role-name $APPSYNC_API_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --assume-role-policy-document file://appsync-trust.json\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncat > appsync-ddb-policy.json <<EOF\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Version\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2012-10-17\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Statement\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"dynamodb:*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:$REGION:*:table/$POST_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:$REGION:*:table/$DOC_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n      \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:dynamodb:$REGION:*:table/$MSG_TABLE\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n    ]\\\\\\\\n  }]\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\nEOF\\\\\\\\naws iam put-role-policy \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --role-name $APPSYNC_API_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --policy-name DDBAccess \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --policy-document file://appsync-ddb-policy.json\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n3. GRAPHQL SCHEMA FILE (schema.graphql)\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\ntype Post @model @auth(rules:[\\\\\\\\n  {allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\\n  {allow: private, operations:[read]}\\\\\\\\n]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  title: String!\\\\\\\\n  body: String\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n  updatedAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ntype Document @model\\\\\\\\n  @auth(rules:[\\\\\\\\n    {allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\\n    {allow: private, operations:[read]}\\\\\\\\n  ]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  title: String!\\\\\\\\n  s3Key: String!\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ntype ContactMessage @model\\\\\\\\n  @auth(rules:[\\\\\\\\n    {allow: public, operations:[create]},\\\\\\\\n    {allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], operations:[read]}\\\\\\\\n  ]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  name: String!\\\\\\\\n  email: AWSEmail!\\\\\\\\n  message: String!\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nschema {\\\\\\\\n  query: Query\\\\\\\\n  mutation: Mutation\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n4. CREATE APPSYNC API & AUTH\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nAPPSYNC_ID=$(aws appsync create-graphql-api \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --name $APPSYNC_NAME \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --authentication-type AMAZON_COGNITO_USER_POOLS \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --user-pool-config userPoolId=$userPoolId,awsRegion=$REGION,defaultAction=ALLOW \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --additional-authentication-providers authenticationType=API_KEY \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --log-config fieldLogLevel=ERROR,cloudWatchLogsRoleArn=arn:aws:iam::$ACCOUNT_ID:role/$APPSYNC_API_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query 'graphqlApi.apiId' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws appsync start-schema-creation --api-id $APPSYNC_ID --definition fileb://schema.graphql\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n5. CREATE DATA SOURCES\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nfor TABLE in $POST_TABLE $DOC_TABLE $MSG_TABLE; do\\\\\\\\n  aws appsync create-data-source \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --api-id $APPSYNC_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --name $TABLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --type AMAZON_DYNAMODB \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --dynamodb-config tableName=$TABLE,awsRegion=$REGION \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n    --service-role-arn arn:aws:iam::$ACCOUNT_ID:role/$APPSYNC_API_ROLE\\\\\\\\ndone\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n6. RESOLVERS\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n# Use Amplify @model transformer output (mapping templates omitted for brevity).\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n7. PIPELINE FUNCTION – SES EMAIL ON ContactMessage.create\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\ncat > contact_email.py <<'PY'\\\\\\\\nimport os,json,boto3\\\\\\\\nses=boto3.client('ses')\\\\\\\\nEMAIL=os.environ['SES_EMAIL']\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ndef handler(event, context):\\\\\\\\n    msg=event['arguments']['input']\\\\\\\\n    ses.send_email(Source=EMAIL,Destination={'ToAddresses':[EMAIL]},Message={\\\\\\\\n        'Subject':{'Data':'New HOA ContactMessage'},\\\\\\\\n        'Body':{'Text':{'Data':json.dumps(msg,indent=2)}}})\\\\\\\\n    return msg\\\\\\\\nPY\\\\\\\\nzip contact_email.zip contact_email.py\\\\\\\\nSES_ROLE=$(aws iam get-role --role-name $APPSYNC_API_ROLE --query 'Role.Arn' --output text)\\\\\\\\naws lambda create-function \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --function-name $SES_FN \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --runtime python3.11 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --zip-file fileb://contact_email.zip \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --handler contact_email.handler \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --role $SES_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --environment Variables=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{SES_EMAIL=board@yourhoadomain.com}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFN_ID=$(aws appsync create-function \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --api-id $APPSYNC_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --name SESMailer \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --function-version 2021-04-15 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --data-source-name NONE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --runtime name=APPSYNC_LAMBDA \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --function-configuration \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lambdaFunctionArn=arn:aws:lambda:$REGION:$ACCOUNT_ID:function:$SES_FN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query 'functionConfiguration.functionId' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws appsync create-resolver \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --api-id $APPSYNC_ID \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --type-name Mutation \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --field-name createContactMessage \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --kind PIPELINE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --pipeline-config functions=[$FN_ID] \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --code \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"## unit resolver generated by @model @\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --runtime name=APPSYNC_JS\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n8. LAMBDA@EDGE (JWT VALIDATOR) & CLOUDFRONT ASSOCIATION\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\ncd edge && zip jwt_validator.zip jwt_validator.py && cd ..\\\\\\\\nEDGE_VER=$(aws lambda publish-version \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --function-name $LAMBDA_EDGE_FN \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --zip-file fileb://edge/jwt_validator.zip \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --handler jwt_validator.handler \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --runtime python3.11 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --role arn:aws:iam::$ACCOUNT_ID:role/$APPSYNC_API_ROLE \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --query Version --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\naws cloudfront update-distribution \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --id $cloudFrontDistributionId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --distribution-config file://cf-config-with-jwt-edge.json \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --if-match $(aws cloudfront get-distribution-config --id $cloudFrontDistributionId --query 'ETag' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n9. PUBLISH OUTPUTS TO SSM FOR FRONTEND\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name $SSM_PREFIX/appsync/apiId     --type String --value $APPSYNC_ID --overwrite\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name $SSM_PREFIX/appsync/endpoint  --type String --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"https://$APPSYNC_ID.appsync-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/graphql\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --overwrite\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name $SSM_PREFIX/appsync/region    --type String --value $REGION --overwrite\\\\\\\\naws ssm put-parameter --name $SSM_PREFIX/appsync/authMode  --type String --value \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AMAZON_COGNITO_USER_POOLS\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" --overwrite\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n10. TEST PLAN\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nAPI_KEY=$(aws appsync create-api-key --api-id $APPSYNC_ID --expires $(( $(date +%s) + 2592000 )) --query 'apiKey.id' --output text)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nget_token(){ aws cognito-idp initiate-auth --auth-flow USER_PASSWORD_AUTH --client-id $userPoolClientId --auth-parameters USERNAME=$1,PASSWORD=$2 --query 'AuthenticationResult.IdToken' --output text; }\\\\\\\\nUSER_TOKEN=$(get_token user@example.com Pass1234!)\\\\\\\\nADMIN_TOKEN=$(get_token admin@example.com Pass1234!)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncurl -s -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Authorization: $USER_TOKEN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"query ListPosts{listPosts{items{id title}}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' https://$APPSYNC_ID.appsync-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/graphql\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncurl -i -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Authorization: $USER_TOKEN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mutation { createPost(input:{title:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hi\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" body:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}){id}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' https://$APPSYNC_ID.appsync-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/graphql\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncurl -s -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Authorization: $ADMIN_TOKEN\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mutation { createPost(input:{title:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hi\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" body:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}){id}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' https://$APPSYNC_ID.appsync-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/graphql\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ncurl -s -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"x-api-key: $API_KEY\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -H \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" -d '{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"query\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"mutation { createContactMessage(input:{name:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Joe\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" email:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"joe@x.com\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" message:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Hi\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}){id}}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}' https://$APPSYNC_ID.appsync-api.$REGION.amazonaws.com/graphql\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEXPECTED RESULTS\\\\\\\\n• listPosts accessible to any authenticated token.  \\\\\\\\n• createPost succeeds only for admin token.  \\\\\\\\n• ContactMessage.create succeeds with public API key and triggers SES email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nFILE MANIFEST\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nschema.graphql  \\\\\\\\ncontact_email.py (+ contact_email.zip)  \\\\\\\\nedge/jwt_validator.py (+ jwt_validator.zip)  \\\\\\\\nappsync-trust.json  \\\\\\\\nappsync-ddb-policy.json  \\\\\\\\ncf-config-with-jwt-edge.json  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n================================================\\\\\\\\nCOST / COMPLEXITY\\\\\\\\n------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n• Reused Cognito, S3, CloudFront – no extra charge.  \\\\\\\\n• AppSync ~$4/mo base + $4 per million operations.  \\\\\\\\n• DynamoDB pay-per-request.  \\\\\\\\n• SES per outgoing email.  \\\\\\\\n• Plan is repeatable & idempotent.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\\nEND OF DELTA DEP\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:39:03.717Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###phase_exec1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: PHASE\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Planning phase produced three Director-level DEPs that now align on a single cohesive architecture: (1) S3+CloudFront static hosting, (2) Cognito authentication, (3) AppSync GraphQL API backed by DynamoDB with SES/Lambda pipeline, (4) Amplify-hosted Next.js front-end.  All resources use deterministic names rooted in the hoa-site project namespace, and every nondeterministic ARN/ID is captured into SSM Parameter Store for later steps.  Each DEP includes exact AWS CLI commands, file manifests, and test scripts.  Cross-team deltas have been reconciled via the approved addenda (arch_rev_1, backend_rev_1) and the original frontend_plan_1 already matches this stack.  No further clarification or design work is required — we now have a single, end-to-end Deterministically Executable Plan ready to be run.  Therefore we request transition to Execution phase so the commands may be issued in the user’s AWS account.\\\",\\n  \\\"depString\\\": \\\"MASTER DEP – HOA WEBSITE (Execution Order)\\\\n================================================\\\\nGLOBAL CONSTANTS\\\\n  REGION=us-east-1\\\\n  PROJECT=hoa-site\\\\n  PARAM_PREFIX=/hoa-site\\\\nAll scripts assume AWS CLI default profile is configured.\\\\n\\\\nSTEP 0 – Bootstrap Helpers\\\\n  aws configure set default.region $REGION\\\\n\\\\nSTEP 1 – Run Architecture Foundation Script (Director R)\\\\n  • Creates SITE_BUCKET, DOCS_BUCKET, LOG_BUCKET (versioned, block-public-access)\\\\n  • Generates CloudFront distribution with OAC; writes Dist ID to SSM\\\\n  • Creates Cognito User Pool + App Client and stores IDs in SSM\\\\n  • Creates empty Lambda (placeholder) + IAM role (will be tightened later)\\\\n  • Creates DynamoDB NewsPosts & Contact tables\\\\n  • Creates AppSync shell (ID only) and attaches those two tables as data sources\\\\n  • All resulting IDs/ARNs stored under $PARAM_PREFIX/*\\\\n\\\\nSTEP 2 – Run Backend/API Script (Director I)\\\\n  • Reads shared IDs from SSM\\\\n  • Generates GraphQL schema, uploads via appsync start-schema-creation\\\\n  • Adds resolvers for Post, Document, ContactMessage\\\\n  • Adds pipeline function (SES email) and Lambda@Edge JWT validator; publishes new Lambda version\\\\n  • Updates CloudFront distribution to attach viewer-request association\\\\n  • Writes AppSync endpoint & auth data back to SSM\\\\n\\\\nSTEP 3 – Front-End / CI-CD (Director Vader)\\\\n  • Locally: create Next.js repo per scaffold\\\\n  • amplify init → env dev → pulls Cognito & AppSync IDs automatically from SSM via Amplify CLI’s `--override` script\\\\n  • amplify add hosting + push – Amplify provisions its deploy role, ties to SITE_BUCKET & CloudFront\\\\n  • GitHub connection finalises continuous deployment\\\\n\\\\nSTEP 4 – Admin Setup & Smoke Tests\\\\n  • Create Cognito group “admins”; add initial board member emails\\\\n  • Run backend test script to validate GraphQL auth rules\\\\n  • Upload a sample PDF to DOCS_BUCKET under `protected/` path, call getPresignedUrl through GraphQL → verify 403 unauth & 200 auth\\\\n  • Front-end Lighthouse accessibility audit ≥ 90\\\\n\\\\nRollback / Idempotency\\\\n  Re-running any script is idempotent because resources have deterministic names; `|| true` guards are present for create commands.\\\\n\\\\nCost Guardrails\\\\n  • S3 + CloudFront (Price Class 100) – pennies per GB for low traffic\\\\n  • AppSync $4 base + pay per request; DynamoDB on-demand; Lambda free tier likely sufficient\\\\n  • AWS Budgets can be added later (out-of-scope for initial execution)\\\\n\\\\nSecurity Highlights\\\\n  • All buckets block public access; CloudFront OAC enforces private origin\\\\n  • Cognito authorises AppSync; mutations limited to admins; ContactMessage create allows public API key only\\\\n  • IAM roles follow least-privilege policies provided in Director scripts\\\\n\\\\nCompletion Criteria\\\\n  • https://<CloudFrontDomain>/ loads site anonymously\\\\n  • Login via Cognito Hosted UI; protected /dues route accessible only after auth\\\\n  • Admin can create News post in Amplify Studio; front page renders it\\\\n  • Contact form submits and board email is received\\\\n================================================\\\"\\n}\\n###phase_exec1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:44:02.892Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"phase_exec1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"DENIED\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Phase shift to EXECUTION was denied by the user.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:44:02.892Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###clarify_denial###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"The user denied the shift to the Execution phase. We need to understand the specific concerns or requested adjustments before proceeding further, so we can revise the plan accordingly and re-seek approval.\\\",\\n  \\\"questions\\\": [\\n    \\\"Could you please let us know what prompted the denial of moving to the Execution phase? For example, are there cost, complexity, security, or timing concerns we should address?\\\",\\n    \\\"Is there any portion of the overall plan (architecture, backend, or frontend) you would like simplified, adjusted, or explained in more detail?\\\",\\n    \\\"Do you have a target monthly budget or other constraints we should explicitly factor into the solution before proceeding?\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"options\\\": []\\n}\\n###clarify_denial###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:44:44.488Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"clarify_denial\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Could you please let us know what prompted the denial of moving to the Execution phase? For example, are there cost, complexity, security, or timing concerns we should address?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Evaluation of the “Deterministically Executable Plan” (DEP) vs. the user’s stated goals  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  Does the DEP deliver the requested functionality? • Public informational pages (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools): YES – a static S3 + CloudFront site can serve them. • Protected pages (Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events): YES – Cognito-authenticated Next.js routes can be gated. • Contact form that emails the board: YES – SES/Lambda pipeline covers this. Gaps between the DEP and the user’s non-technical-user requirements • Content updates.  All pages live in a Next.js/Amplify repo.  Updating “News & Events” or editing minutes means: cloning the repo, editing Markdown/JSX, committing + pushing to Git. That workflow is not “simple and user-friendly” for someone who “knows pretty much nothing about technology”. No CMS (e.g., Amplify Studio CMS, AWS Headless CMS, or third-party headless CMS) or WYSIWYG editor is included. • Day-to-day admin UI. Cognito user management requires console or CLI knowledge; no custom admin panel is specified. • On-boarding instructions. The DEP has exhaustive AWS CLI commands but zero end-user documentation (“how the secretary uploads minutes”, “how to reset a resident’s password”, etc.). Technical soundness • Architecture is modern and secure; deterministic names + SSM tracking are good DevOps practices. • Test scripts and parameterization show maturity. Operational fit & cost • Monthly bill: CloudFront + AppSync + DynamoDB + SES + Lambda + Cognito may be overkill for a low-traffic HOA site. • Ongoing maintenance (patching, IAM, cost monitoring) falls on the HOA, contradicting the “non-technical” profile. Compliance with the stated “no further design work” assertion • From a purely technical execution standpoint the DEP is runnable. • From a solution-fit standpoint, more design work is still needed (chiefly around content management and resident admin UX). Suggested remediations a) Add a CMS layer: • Easiest AWS-native: Amplify Studio CMS generates a visual content editor for static/Next.js pages; or • Drop-in headless options: Netlify CMS, Sanity, or Strapi running on a small ECS/Fargate task. b) Provide a lightweight admin portal for: • Uploading documents (minutes, reports) to a “protected” S3 folder automatically surfaced in the UI. • Managing Cognito users (approve, disable, resend invite). c) Produce non-technical runbooks: • “Posting a news item”, “Adding a new resident”, “Resetting a password”, etc., with screenshots. d) Trim stack for cost/complexity if traffic is low: • Replace AppSync + DynamoDB with simply signed S3 URLs for document download and a contact form Lambda. • Use Amazon Simple Email Service directly from the form POST. Overall score Technical completeness: 9/10 User-fit completeness: 5/10 Execution readiness: 8/10 Total alignment with user’s goals: 6/10  Conclusion The DEP is well-crafted for an engineering team but only partially satisfies the HOA president’s real-world needs. It should not yet move to execution without adding a user-friendly content-management layer, clearer administrative workflows, and simplified maintenance instructions. (Signed, Partagaz D Analysis Group)\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Is there any portion of the overall plan (architecture, backend, or frontend) you would like simplified, adjusted, or explained in more detail?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N/A\\\\\\\",\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Do you have a target monthly budget or other constraints we should explicitly factor into the solution before proceeding?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"N/A\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:44:44.488Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###rec_docs###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"justification\\\": \\\"Partagaz D feedback highlights a significant usability gap for non-technical HOA admins and residents. A senior-level agent is needed to own creation of clear, screenshot-rich runbooks / user guides (posting news, uploading minutes, managing residents, resetting passwords, etc.) and to define ongoing operational procedures. This warrants a Director-rank \\\\\\\"Documentation & Training\\\\\\\" role who will coordinate with the existing technical leads and produce artefacts that accompany the deployment.\\\",\\n  \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Documentation & Training\\\"\\n}\\n###rec_docs###\\n\\n###order_frontend_rev2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend_rev_2\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Partagaz D flagged lack of a truly non-technical CMS/admin experience. Revise your DEP with the following additions (delta only):\\\\n\\\\n1. ADMIN PORTAL & CMS\\\\n   • Add /admin route (protected by Cognito group \\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\") presenting a dashboard with cards for:\\\\n       – \\\\\\\"News & Events\\\\\\\" (list, create, edit, delete posts via Amplify DataStore GraphQL mutations).\\\\n       – \\\\\\\"Documents\\\\\\\" (upload PDF to S3 protected path via Amplify Storage.put; surface metadata via GraphQL Document model).\\\\n       – \\\\\\\"Residents\\\\\\\" (link opens Amplify Admin UI › User management in a new tab).\\\\n   • For News & Events editing, integrate a rich-text WYSIWYG ( @tinymce/tinymce-react ) component so content is edited visually—no Markdown required.\\\\n\\\\n2. WYSIWYG & FORMS IMPLEMENTATION\\\\n   • Modify Post model to include `contentHtml` string field to store TinyMCE output.\\\\n   • Provide React component snippets (max 1 file each) for NewsEditor.tsx and DocsUploader.tsx; include amplification of Storage.put and creating Document entry.\\\\n\\\\n3. AMPLIFY STUDIO CONTENT MANAGER\\\\n   • Document the one-time steps to enable Studio → Content → Post & Document collections, grant admins group access, and share invitation links with board members.\\\\n   • Explain how Studio gives a GUI for non-technical edits in parallel to the in-app admin dashboard (either path acceptable).\\\\n\\\\n4. UX POLISH\\\\n   • Add quick-links in Navbar for logged-in admins to reach dashboard.\\\\n   • Ensure protected pages display friendly \\\\\\\"You must log in\\\\\\\" message instead of blank redirect.\\\\n\\\\n5. UPDATE DEP SECTIONS\\\\n   • Provide revised folder structure and any new Amplify commands (`amplify add storage`, `amplify push`) but only list the deltas—not the full earlier DEP.\\\\n   • Update accessibility statement for new components.\\\\n\\\\nReturn your delta-focused DEP update in report sequencing frontend_rev_2.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_frontend_rev2###\\n\\n###order_backend_rev2###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend_rev_2\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"We must cement a non-technical CMS flow and simplify Cognito admin tasks per Partagaz D feedback. Provide a delta DEP update covering:\\\\n\\\\n1. GRAPHQL SCHEMA UPDATES\\\\n   • Extend Post model: add `contentHtml: String`.\\\\n   • Add S3 object key field to Document model (already present but ensure correct field name: `s3Key`).\\\\n\\\\n2. STORAGE FOR DOCUMENT UPLOADS\\\\n   • Use Amplify CLI `amplify add storage` (or equivalent CLI) to create an S3 bucket pathway `protected/documents/` with auth rules: only admins can Put, any authenticated user can Get.\\\\n   • Provide IAM policies updates and example pre-signed upload / download workflows that Frontend will call.\\\\n\\\\n3. COGNITO ADMIN WORKFLOWS\\\\n   • Document (a) how to add/remove users via Amplify Admin UI, (b) automatic email invite process, and (c) password reset flow. Provide CLI equivalents for power users but emphasise GUI path.\\\\n\\\\n4. COST SIMPLIFICATION CHECK\\\\n   • Analyse monthly cost with AppSync + DynamoDB + Amplify Studio CMS vs. simpler alternative. Confirm current design remains <≈$25/mo at low traffic and note break-even points.\\\\n\\\\n5. RUNBOOK INPUTS\\\\n   • List the exact steps/screens the forthcoming Documentation Director should capture (URLs, menu clicks) so their runbooks align.\\\\n\\\\nReturn delta DEP in report backend_rev_2.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_backend_rev2###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:47:04.323Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rec_docs\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Meero (5) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_frontend_rev2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order frontend_rev_2 from agent 3: DELTA UPDATE – DEP FRONTEND (NON-TECHNICAL CMS EXPERIENCE)\\\\\\\\nSequence ID: frontend_rev_2  \\\\\\\\nAuthor: Vader (Director)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n────────────────────────────────────────\\\\\\\\nΔ1. ADMIN PORTAL & CMS ADDITION\\\\\\\\n• New protected route: /admin  (Next.js src/app/admin/protected/page.tsx). Guarded by _authGuard plus Cognito group check: user.signInUserSession.idToken.payload[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cognito:groups\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"] includes \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".  \\\\\\\\n• AdminDashboard.tsx displays three cards (News & Events, Documents, Residents).   \\\\\\\\n   – News & Events → /admin/news  (list + NewsEditor).  \\\\\\\\n   – Documents → /admin/documents (DocsUploader + list).  \\\\\\\\n   – Residents → external link: Amplify Admin UI › User management (`https://<appId>.admin.amplifyapp.com/user-management`). Opens in new tab.  \\\\\\\\n• Friendly message for non-admin authenticated users: “You need administrator rights to access this page.”\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ2. WYSIWYG & FORMS IMPLEMENTATION\\\\\\\\nGraphQL Post model amendment (amplify/backend/api/schema.graphql):\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\ntype Post @model @auth(rules:[{allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"], operations:[create,update,delete,read]},{allow: public, operations:[read]}]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  title: String!\\\\\\\\n  contentHtml: String!    # TinyMCE output stored as HTML\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nRun deterministically:\\\\\\\\n`amplify api gql-compile`  (auto–executed inside `amplify push`)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nComponent Snippets  (1 file each – placed in src/components/)\\\\\\\\n--- NewsEditor.tsx ---\\\\\\\\n```tsx\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"use client\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { useState } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"react\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { Editor } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"@tinymce/tinymce-react\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { API, graphqlOperation } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aws-amplify\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { createPost, updatePost } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"graphql/mutations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { Post } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"../models\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport default function NewsEditor({ existing }: { existing?: Post }) {\\\\\\\\n  const [title, setTitle] = useState(existing?.title ?? \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n  const [contentHtml, setContentHtml] = useState(existing?.contentHtml ?? \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n  const save = async () => {\\\\\\\\n    const input = { id: existing?.id, title, contentHtml };\\\\\\\\n    const mutation = existing ? updatePost : createPost;\\\\\\\\n    await API.graphql(graphqlOperation(mutation, { input }));\\\\\\\\n    alert(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Saved\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n  };\\\\\\\\n  return (\\\\\\\\n    <div className=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"space-y-4\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">\\\\\\\\n      <input\\\\\\\\n        aria-label=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Post title\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n        className=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"w-full border p-2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n        value={title}\\\\\\\\n        onChange={e => setTitle(e.target.value)}\\\\\\\\n        placeholder=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Title\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n      />\\\\\\\\n      <Editor\\\\\\\\n        apiKey=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"no-api-key\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n        value={contentHtml}\\\\\\\\n        onEditorChange={setContentHtml}\\\\\\\\n        init={{ menubar: false, height: 300, toolbar_mode: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wrap\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" }}\\\\\\\\n      />\\\\\\\\n      <button className=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"btn-primary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" onClick={save} aria-label=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Save post\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">Save</button>\\\\\\\\n    </div>\\\\\\\\n  );\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--- DocsUploader.tsx ---\\\\\\\\n```tsx\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"use client\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { useState } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"react\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { Storage, API, graphqlOperation } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aws-amplify\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\nimport { createDocument } from \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"graphql/mutations\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\";\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nexport default function DocsUploader() {\\\\\\\\n  const [file, setFile] = useState<File | null>(null);\\\\\\\\n  const upload = async () => {\\\\\\\\n    if (!file) return;\\\\\\\\n    const key = `protected/${file.name}`;\\\\\\\\n    await Storage.put(key, file, { contentType: file.type, level: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"protected\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" });\\\\\\\\n    await API.graphql(graphqlOperation(createDocument, {\\\\\\\\n      input: { name: file.name, s3Key: key, uploadedAt: new Date().toISOString() }\\\\\\\\n    }));\\\\\\\\n    alert(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Uploaded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\");\\\\\\\\n  };\\\\\\\\n  return (\\\\\\\\n    <div className=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"space-y-2\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">\\\\\\\\n      <input type=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" accept=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"application/pdf\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" onChange={e => setFile(e.target.files?.[0] ?? null)} />\\\\\\\\n      <button className=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"btn-primary\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" onClick={upload} aria-label=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Upload document\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\">Upload</button>\\\\\\\\n    </div>\\\\\\\\n  );\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ3. AMPLIFY STUDIO CONTENT MANAGER – ONE-TIME STEPS\\\\\\\\n1. `amplify console --appId <appId>` → open Amplify Console, click “Launch Studio”.  \\\\\\\\n2. In Studio, enable “Content”. Two collections auto-detected from schema: Post, Document.  \\\\\\\\n3. Grant access: Settings → Access management → Add Cognito group → `admins` (CRUD).  \\\\\\\\n4. Invite board members: Users → Invite → enter emails; Studio sends magic-link with limited content access.  \\\\\\\\n5. Editors can now add Posts/Docs via browser GUI without logging into GitHub or app; changes sync through DataStore instantly, parallel to in-app admin dashboard.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ4. UX POLISH\\\\\\\\n• Navbar.tsx now conditionally renders “Dashboard” link when `groups?.includes(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")`.  \\\\\\\\n• _authGuard.tsx updated: if unauthenticated → render centered message “Please log in to access this page” with `<Authenticator/>` component fallback, instead of silent redirect.  \\\\\\\\n• For colour-blind admins, dashboard card icons include text labels.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ5. REVISED FOLDER STRUCTURE (NEW/CHANGED ONLY)\\\\\\\\nsrc/app/\\\\\\\\n  └─ admin/protected/\\\\\\\\n       ├─ page.tsx               # AdminDashboard wrapper\\\\\\\\n       ├─ news/page.tsx          # list & <NewsEditor/>\\\\\\\\n       └─ documents/page.tsx     # list & <DocsUploader/>\\\\\\\\nsrc/components/\\\\\\\\n  ├─ AdminDashboard.tsx\\\\\\\\n  ├─ NewsEditor.tsx  (NEW)\\\\\\\\n  └─ DocsUploader.tsx (NEW)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ6. NEW AMPLIFY COMMANDS\\\\\\\\n1. `amplify add storage`  \\\\\\\\n   – Service: S3  \\\\\\\\n   – Friendly name: docfiles  \\\\\\\\n   – Access: Auth & Guest (read), Admin group (create/update)  \\\\\\\\n   – Auth/guest permissions: Auth CRUD, Guest read  \\\\\\\\n2. `amplify push --yes`  (provisions Storage, updates GraphQL schema, deploys)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nΔ7. ACCESSIBILITY STATEMENT UPDATE\\\\\\\\n• TinyMCE initialized with `a11ychecker` plugin, toolbar role=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"toolbar\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", buttons have `aria-label`.  \\\\\\\\n• DocsUploader input tagged `aria-label=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Upload document\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`.  \\\\\\\\n• Dashboard cards are <button> elements with role=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"link\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and high-contrast focus ring (Tailwind focus-visible).  \\\\\\\\n• Admin routes maintain keyboard navigation order; success/error alerts announced via `aria-live=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"polite\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"` regions.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nEND OF DELTA UPDATE\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_backend_rev2\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order backend_rev_2 from agent 2: ==============================\\\\\\\\nDELTA DEP  –  backend_rev_2\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\\nAuthor: I (Director – Backend & Auth)\\\\\\\\nPurpose: Apply Partagaz D feedback – CMS flow & Cognito admin simplification\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. GRAPHQL SCHEMA CHANGES (schema.graphql)\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n# Only the affected bits are shown.\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\ntype Post @model @auth(rules:[\\\\\\\\n  {allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},\\\\\\\\n  {allow: private, operations:[read]}\\\\\\\\n]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  title: String!\\\\\\\\n  body: String\\\\\\\\n  contentHtml: String          # <-- NEW FIELD (rich-text HTML)\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n  updatedAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\ntype Document @model\\\\\\\\n  @auth(rules:[\\\\\\\\n    {allow: groups, groups:[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admins\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]},        # create/update/delete\\\\\\\\n    {allow: private, operations:[read]}         # any logged-in user may query\\\\\\\\n  ]) {\\\\\\\\n  id: ID!\\\\\\\\n  title: String!\\\\\\\\n  s3Key: String!              # <-- ENSURE CORRECT NAME (unchanged)\\\\\\\\n  createdAt: AWSDateTime\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n• No resolver changes required; Amplify Transformer re-generates mapping templates automatically after schema push.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n2. STORAGE FOR DOCUMENT UPLOADS\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. RESOURCE CREATION (deterministic)\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nAMPLIFY_ENV=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"prod\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nAMPLIFY_APP=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"hoa-site\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nAMPLIFY_BUCKET=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"${AMPLIFY_APP}-protected-docs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\namplify add storage \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --bucketName $AMPLIFY_BUCKET \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --service S3 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --accessType authenticated \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --prefix \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"protected/documents/\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --authConfig \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"adminUpload\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"readAccess\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"auth\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"uploadAccess\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"admin:groups\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n# followed by:\\\\\\\\namplify push --yes\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nThe CLI generates:\\\\\\\\n• S3 bucket (if not already existing) named exactly `$AMPLIFY_BUCKET`.\\\\\\\\n• Two IAM roles attached to the Cognito identity pool:\\\\\\\\n  – **Admin** (Cognito group *admins*): s3:PutObject & GetObject on `protected/documents/*`.\\\\\\\\n  – **Authenticated** (any): s3:GetObject on `protected/documents/*`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nIf we keep the earlier *protectedBucket* (Parameter Store) we simply apply **policy-only**; the above `bucketName` flag points to that existing bucket so no extra bucket is created, maintaining determinism.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. POLICY STATEMENTS (least-privilege delta)\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n# For admin-role attached to IdentityPool\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:PutObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:GetObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::${protectedBucket}/protected/documents/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n# For auth-role\\\\\\\\n{\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Effect\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Allow\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Action\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"s3:GetObject\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Resource\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"arn:aws:s3:::${protectedBucket}/protected/documents/*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\nC. PRESIGNED WORKFLOWS (used by Frontend)\\\\\\\\n• **Upload (admin only)**\\\\\\\\n  1. Admin obtains Cognito *IdToken* (already includes group claim).\\\\\\\\n  2. Frontend calls AppSync *getAdminS3Presign* (new Lambda resolver or local call) which generates:\\\\\\\\n  ```python\\\\\\\\n  url = s3.generate_presigned_url('put_object',\\\\\\\\n        Params={'Bucket': protectedBucket,\\\\\\\\n                'Key': f'protected/documents/{uuid4()}.pdf',\\\\\\\\n                'ContentType':'application/pdf'},\\\\\\\\n        ExpiresIn=900)\\\\\\\\n  ```\\\\\\\\n  3. Browser `PUT` directly to S3 with returned URL.\\\\\\\\n  4. Immediately after upload, admin executes GraphQL mutation `createDocument` with `s3Key` of the object.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n• **Download (any authenticated user)**\\\\\\\\n  1. User queries `listDocuments`.\\\\\\\\n  2. Frontend requests presigned GET using the existing Lambda (or new “getDocUrl”) with Cognito token; only the *GetObject* policy is required.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n3. COGNITO ADMIN WORKFLOWS  –  **Human-Friendly CMS Path**\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. **Amplify Admin UI (GUI first)**\\\\\\\\n   1. Navigate to https://us-east-1.admin.amplify.aws.\\\\\\\\n   2. Select *hoa-site* app → *User Management*.\\\\\\\\n   3. Click `Invite users` → supply email address + *admins* group if necessary.\\\\\\\\n      • AWS sends automatic *Account invitation* email containing temp password.\\\\\\\\n   4. Remove user: select user row → `Disable` or `Delete`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. **Automatic Email Invite Flow**\\\\\\\\n   – Handled automatically by Cognito when `AdminCreateUser` is executed (GUI or CLI).\\\\\\\\n   – Email includes a `CONFIRM` link; user must set new password on first sign-in.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. **Password Reset (Self-Service)**\\\\\\\\n   1. User clicks *Forgot Password* on the login page (Amplify UI component).\\\\\\\\n   2. Cognito emails a 6-digit code.\\\\\\\\n   3. User submits code + new password, completing reset.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. **CLI Equivalents (power users/devops)**\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n# Create / invite\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp admin-create-user \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --user-pool-id $userPoolId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --username john@example.com \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --user-attributes Name=email,Value=john@example.com \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --desired-delivery-mediums EMAIL \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --message-action SUPPRESS  # omit to send default invite email\\\\\\\\n# Add to admins group\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp admin-add-user-to-group \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --user-pool-id $userPoolId \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --username john@example.com \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --group-name admins\\\\\\\\n# Force password reset at next sign-in\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp admin-set-user-password \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --user-pool-id $userPoolId --username john@example.com \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  --password 'TempPass#1' --permanent false\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n4. COST SIMPLIFICATION CHECK\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nAssumptions: <5K monthly site visits, <200 document downloads, <100 GraphQL writes.\\\\\\\\n• AppSync: $4 base + (5K×0.0004) ≈ $6  →  $10\\\\\\\\n• DynamoDB: reads/writes fit in free/low tier → <$2.\\\\\\\\n• S3 storage: 1 GB documents → $0.023.\\\\\\\\n• S3 transfer (CloudFront takes most): negligible.\\\\\\\\n• CloudFront + Lambda@Edge (~1M viewer-req): $8.\\\\\\\\n• SES (100 emails): <$0.10.\\\\\\\\n• Amplify Admin UI (no charge) / Amplify Hosting handled by Frontend budget.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTOTAL ≈ **$20/month**. Alternative (single Lambda REST vs. AppSync) would save ~$4 but loses CMS benefits & fine-grained auth; break-even once AppSync ops exceed ~10 M per month (~$40). Current design remains comfortably below the $25 target at projected traffic.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\n5. RUNBOOK INPUTS FOR DOCUMENTATION DIRECTOR\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nA. **User Management**\\\\\\\\n   – URL: https://us-east-1.admin.amplify.aws → *hoa-site* → *User Management*\\\\\\\\n   – Click flow: `Invite users` → enter email → assign *admins* group.\\\\\\\\n   – Remove/disable: select user row → kebab menu → `Disable` or `Delete`.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nB. **Posts & Documents CMS**\\\\\\\\n   – Same Amplify Admin UI: *Content* → *Post* model.\\\\\\\\n   – Create/Update fields: title, body, contentHtml.\\\\\\\\n   – For Document: upload file via Upload button (uses storage rules) → s3Key auto-attached → save.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nC. **Password Reset Walkthrough**\\\\\\\\n   – Login page → `Forgot Password` → email code entry → new password.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nD. **S3 Document Upload via CLI (backup method)**\\\\\\\\n   – `aws s3 cp file.pdf s3://$protectedBucket/protected/documents/ --profile admin`\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nE. **Monitoring / Logs**\\\\\\\\n   – CloudWatch Logs → `/aws/appsync/apis/$APPSYNC_ID` and Lambda@Edge logs group.\\\\\\\\n   – AppSync Dashboard metrics.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\\\\\\\\nNO INFRASTRUCTURE COMMAND EXECUTION REQUIRED AT THIS MOMENT – Only schema & policy updates awaiting Amplify push.\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\\nEND OF DELTA DEP\\\\\\\\n==============================\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:47:04.323Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###order_docs_runbooks###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 5,\\n  \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"docs_runbooks_1\\\",\\n  \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"As Director of Documentation & Training, please prepare a comprehensive, non-technical runbook suite for HOA board members and residents.  Produce clear, screenshot-referenced PDFs/markdown outlines that will accompany the final deployment.  \\\\n\\\\nDELIVERABLES (one file/section each; bullet-style is fine):\\\\n1. \\\\\\\"Posting News & Events\\\\\\\": step-by-step guide for using the in-app /admin → News & Amplify Studio Content Manager to create, edit, delete posts with TinyMCE.  \\\\n2. \\\\\\\"Uploading Meeting Minutes & Financial Reports\\\\\\\": how to use DocsUploader component or Studio Document collection to upload/download PDFs.  \\\\n3. \\\\\\\"Managing Residents\\\\\\\": invite/remove/disable users via Amplify Admin UI and basic CLI equivalents.  \\\\n4. \\\\\\\"Password Reset & Self-Service\\\\\\\": what residents see and do during forgot-password flow.  \\\\n5. \\\\\\\"Contact-Us Messages\\\\\\\": where board members read submitted messages (AppSync ContactMessage list) and e-mail notification expectations.  \\\\n6. \\\\\\\"Monthly Quick Health Check\\\\\\\": simple checklist (cost dashboard, CloudWatch alarms, SES bounce report) that any layperson can follow.  \\\\n\\\\nSTYLE GUIDELINES  \\\\n• Assume reader has no AWS or Git background.  \\\\n• Use plain English, numbered steps, and bold UI labels.  \\\\n• Where screenshots are referenced, include placeholder text like \\\\\\\"[screenshot: Invite Users button]\\\\\\\" that engineers can later capture.  \\\\n• Keep each section <2 pages.  \\\\n\\\\nReturn the runbook drafts (markdown or plaintext) in your report under sequence docs_runbooks_1.\\\"\\n}\\n###order_docs_runbooks###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:48:15.012Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"order_docs_runbooks\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Report for order docs_runbooks_1 from agent 5: # HOA Portal – Runbook Suite (Drafts)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 1. Posting News & Events\\\\\\\\n**Goal:** Board members publish timely announcements that appear in the resident-facing “News & Events” feed.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. **Sign in** to the admin area → **/admin**.  \\\\\\\\n2. From the left sidebar choose **Content → News**.  \\\\\\\\n3. Click **+ New Post**. *[screenshot: New Post button]*  \\\\\\\\n4. In the **Title** box, type a short headline.  \\\\\\\\n5. In the **Body** area (TinyMCE editor):  \\\\\\\\n   a. Type or paste text.  \\\\\\\\n   b. Use toolbar for **Bold**, **Links**, **Insert Image**, etc. *[screenshot: TinyMCE toolbar]*  \\\\\\\\n6. (Optional) **Add Cover Image** by dragging a file or clicking **Upload**.  \\\\\\\\n7. **Publish** options:  \\\\\\\\n   • Click **Save Draft** to keep private.  \\\\\\\\n   • Click **Publish** to go live immediately. *[screenshot: Publish dropdown]*  \\\\\\\\n8. **Edit** an existing post: hover row → **… → Edit**; make changes → **Update**.  \\\\\\\\n9. **Delete** a post: hover row → **… → Delete → Confirm**.  \\\\\\\\n10. **Verify** on resident site home page that the post appears/updates correctly.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 2. Uploading Meeting Minutes & Financial Reports\\\\\\\\n**Goal:** Make PDF documents available for residents to view/download.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. In-App DocsUploader Component\\\\\\\\n1. Navigate to **/board/documents** (Board Portal).  \\\\\\\\n2. Click **Upload Document**. *[screenshot: Upload Document button]*  \\\\\\\\n3. **Drag-and-drop** or **Browse** to a PDF.  \\\\\\\\n4. Select a **Category** (e.g., “Meeting Minutes”, “Financials”).  \\\\\\\\n5. Click **Save**.  \\\\\\\\n6. Confirm the new row appears with **Download** link.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. Amplify Studio – Document Collection\\\\\\\\n1. Open **Amplify Studio** → **Content → Documents**.  \\\\\\\\n2. Click **Create Docs**.  \\\\\\\\n3. Fill in **Name**, **Year/Month**, and **Upload File**. *[screenshot: File picker]*  \\\\\\\\n4. Click **Save**.  \\\\\\\\n5. Residents instantly see the file under **Documents** in the app.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### C. Replace or Remove\\\\\\\\n• To update, click the doc row → **Replace File** → choose new PDF → **Save**.  \\\\\\\\n• To delete, select row → **Delete 1 item → Confirm**.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 3. Managing Residents\\\\\\\\n**Goal:** Control who has portal access.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### A. Amplify Admin UI (Recommended)\\\\\\\\n1. Open **Amplify Console** → your app → **Admin UI**.  \\\\\\\\n2. Choose **Users** tab.  \\\\\\\\n3. **Invite User**:  \\\\\\\\n   a. Click **Invite Users**. *[screenshot: Invite Users button]*  \\\\\\\\n   b. Enter email(s); choose **Resident** or **Board** group.  \\\\\\\\n   c. Click **Send Invite** (email contains one-time link).  \\\\\\\\n4. **Disable / Enable**: select user → **Actions → Disable / Enable** → **Confirm**.  \\\\\\\\n5. **Remove**: select user → **Delete User → Confirm** (removes login entirely).  \\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n### B. CLI Equivalent (optional for tech helpers)\\\\\\\\n```bash\\\\\\\\n# List users\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp list-users --user-pool-id <POOL_ID>\\\\\\\\n# Disable user\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp admin-disable-user --user-pool-id <POOL_ID> --username user@example.com\\\\\\\\n# Delete user\\\\\\\\naws cognito-idp admin-delete-user --user-pool-id <POOL_ID> --username user@example.com\\\\\\\\n```\\\\\\\\n*You can find **POOL_ID** in Admin UI → **User management → Pool details***.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 4. Password Reset & Self-Service\\\\\\\\n1. On login screen, residents click **Forgot password?**. *[screenshot: Forgot link]*  \\\\\\\\n2. Enter **Email** → **Send Code**.  \\\\\\\\n3. Check inbox for **reset code (6 digits)**; if not found, check spam.  \\\\\\\\n4. Return to app → enter **Code** + **New Password** → **Submit**.  \\\\\\\\n5. Success message appears; click **Back to Sign In** and log in with new password.  \\\\\\\\n6. If code expires (15 min) or three failed attempts, repeat step 1.  \\\\\\\\n7. Still stuck? Board can **Disable** then **Enable** the user (see Section 3) to force a new email.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 5. Contact-Us Messages\\\\\\\\n1. Board receives an **email notification** for each submission (subject: “New Contact-Us message”).  \\\\\\\\n2. To view all, sign in to **/admin** → **Content → ContactMessages**.  \\\\\\\\n3. Columns show **Name, Email, Subject, Date**.  \\\\\\\\n4. Click a row to open full **Message**. *[screenshot: Message detail]*  \\\\\\\\n5. Use resident’s email to reply directly from your email client (portal does not send replies).  \\\\\\\\n6. When processed, mark **Status → Closed** to hide from default list.  \\\\\\\\n7. Data is stored in AppSync **ContactMessage** table for audit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n## 6. Monthly Quick Health Check\\\\\\\\nA 10-minute checklist to ensure the portal is healthy & cost-effective.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n| # | Task | How | Expected OK |\\\\\\\\n|---|------|-----|-------------|\\\\\\\\n|1| **Billing – Cost Explorer** | AWS console → **Billing → Cost Explorer → Monthly costs** | Matches budget; spike ≤10 % |\\\\\\\\n|2| **Budgets Alerts** | Billing → **Budgets** | No “breached” alerts |\\\\\\\\n|3| **CloudWatch Alarms** | CloudWatch → **Alarms** | All in **OK** state |\\\\\\\\n|4| **App Health** | Amplify Console → **All apps** | Green check on build & prod branches |\\\\\\\\n|5| **SES Bounce Rate** | SES → **Sending Statistics** | Bounce rate < 5 % |\\\\\\\\n|6| **Error Logs** | CloudWatch → **Log groups → /aws/amplify/** | No repetitive ERROR entries |\\\\\\\\n|7| **Domain & SSL** | Route 53 → **Hosted zones**; ACM → **Certificates** | Records valid, certificates < 30 days to renewal |\\\\\\\\n|8| **Backup Review** | S3 → **Backups** bucket | Last backup timestamp < 24 h |\\\\\\\\n|9| **User Feedback** | Check Contact-Us list (Section 5) | No unresolved critical issues |\\\\\\\\n|10| **Document Currency** | /board/documents | Latest meeting minutes & financials present |\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n*Record any issues in board meeting agenda and assign follow-ups.*\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n---\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n_End of drafts – ready for screenshot capture & PDF export._\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-22T19:48:15.012Z###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:state":"error"},"displayName":"generate","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":2,"message":"429 Request too large for o3 in organization org-WujsL8iohmbso5xQUsyhs6VN on tokens per min (TPM): Limit 30000, Requested 30372. The input or output tokens must be reduced in order to run successfully. Visit https://platform.openai.c